### UI resolution + per-resolution asset URI substitution.
### See docs/architecture/build-and-tooling.md (icon resolution pipeline) and
### resources/icons/README.md.
###
### ui_resolutions=fhd: app is designed at 1920x1080 design coords; the OS
### auto-downsamples the framebuffer to 720p / 480p on HD/SD devices. We
### canNOT declare ui_resolutions=hd,fhd without first rewriting every
### layout coordinate to be runtime-computed from m.global.device.uiResolution
### — declaring both tells Roku NOT to autoscale and to use the device's
### native coord space, which causes our 1920-wide elements to overflow on
### HD devices. Tracked as tech-debt slug hd-native-layout-refactor.
###
### uri_resolution_autosub rewrites $$RES$$ in any image URI to sd/hd/fhd at
### load time. Currently of limited value because the OS holds rendering at
### FHD coord space, but the per-resolution PNG assets are in place as
### foundation work for the eventual layout refactor.
ui_resolutions=fhd
uri_resolution_autosub=$$RES$$,sd,hd,fhd

